  "id": "amh",
  "term": "AMH",
  "definition": "AMH stands for Adaptive Market Hypothesis, the idea that investors are not fully rational but adjust their behavior over time. In this view, biases such as herding and overconfidence can continue and change as people respond to social and personal learning factors.",
